      {
         "id": "d",
         "prompt": "Since \\( f'(x) > 0 \\) for \\( x > -1 \\), \\( f \\) has an inverse function \\( k \\). Find \\( k'(5) \\), and use the line tangent to the graph of \\( k \\) at \\( x = 5 \\) to approximate \\( k(4) \\).",
         "setup_required": false,
         "answer_latex": "k(4) \\approx \\frac{5}{3}",
         "worked_solution": [
            {
               "text": "k(5) = 2 because f(2) = 5, and the derivative of the inverse is the reciprocal slope.",
               "latex": "k'(5) = \\frac{1}{f'(2)} = \\frac{1}{3}"
            },
            {
               "text": "Tangent line to k through (5, 2).",
               "latex": "y = 2 + \\frac{1}{3}(x - 5)"
            },
            {
               "text": "Evaluate at x = 4.",
               "latex": "k(4) \\approx 2 - \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{5}{3}"
            }
